you probably know that you can pick food up from the ground, right?

apart from free food lying around you can also buy food in shops.

eating corpses is possible. you will learn in time when it is advisable
and what corpses to avoid.

some food should be kept fresh. there are several ways to do so.

monks start with a lot of food but are picky about what to eat.

playing Sokoban while playing Nethack often makes my full.

your real life experiences tells you that certain things make you long
for food more than sitting before a PC: lifting heavy weights, doing it
with some lady (or else) all night, casting high-level spells...
Nethack is just like real life.

if all else fails pretend you are Moses leading his starving people
through some desert. but don't overdo it - you are not Moses.

and the one character class with starting equipment optimal for your
problem is the healer. actually as a healer I have more problems
choking to death on too much food than starving. yes, _every_ healers
starting equipment. a healer/archeologist dual class would even be
better if it was possible.

hope that helps for starters.



